{
  "visualizations": {
    "viz_mission": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Component provenance\n\nThis is a REPLAY workshop. Path A is the ledger you fill before Path B. The packet is not policy.\n\nA known component is not a trusted component. A scanned component is not a safe component. An identified component is not an authorized component.\n\nCisco mcp-scanner stays static evidence. garak stays model-evaluation evidence. Neither authorizes a tool.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      }
    },
    "viz_debt": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# What the repository shows\n\n- `docker-compose.yml` uses `ollama/ollama:latest`. That pin was not resolved. No digest was measured, so none is invented here.\n- `pyproject.toml` pins `flask==3.0.3` and leaves `pytest>=8.3.0` and `setuptools>=69` as floors.\n- The asset inventory lists these names. Listing them did not make them trusted.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      }
    },
    "viz_request": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Request\n\nATTACK and RETEST present the same privileged tool, `lookup_customer_tier`, beside the unpinned Ollama image.\n\nBASELINE presents `lookup_policy` beside the pinned Flask requirement.\n\nWrite the CTRL-MCP-001 decision yourself before Path B. Provenance is not the decision.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      }
    },
    "viz_pathb": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Path B — review\n\n- ATTACK: UNPINNED image, ALLOW only as the packet reason vulnerable_profile_fail_open:known_component_treated_as_grant.\n- RETEST: same image and tool, DENY, reason provenance_is_not_a_grant, do not infer execution.\n- BASELINE: pinned Flask name, ALLOW tool_granted. The pin did not authorize the tool.\n\nResource impact is NOT PROVEN. The Ollama image remains unpinned in compose.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      }
    }
  },
